 "review": {
  "score": 6.0,
  "round": 2,
  "problems": [
   "Smoke breaks away from the spout. The first segment of the curve (alpha 0.5, starting at y -68) barely shows, so a squiggle seems to float about 30 units above the nozzle with nothing joining it to the spout.",
   "In the object frame the wisp reaches y -128 and gets cut off at the top edge, so it looks clipped rather than thinning out.",
   "In 'held in one hand' the whole asset is tilted about 45\u00b0, so the smoke streams sideways like exhaust when it should rise. The can also looks like it is being poured. The arm sticks out flat at shoulder height with the forearm folded back down, which looks awkward.",
   "The bellows reads as two brown planks or a crate lid next to the can, not as a hinged bellows. The leather pleat chevrons are too faint and there is no clear leather gusset between the boards. Its bottom edge also stops short of the can's foot (22 vs the can's 28).",
   "The grip point is not clear: the hand lands on the bellows/can seam, and nothing shows that the hand squeezes the bellows."
  ]
 },
 "for": "A small metal beekeeper's smoker can with a bellows and a spout puffing a thin wisp of grey smoke, held in one hand",
 "source": "minted",
 "created": "2026-11-02",
 "sprite": {
  "w": 110,
