 },
 "sprite_review": {
  "score": 6.0,
  "problems": [
   "The brief asks for 'a thin wisp of grey smoke' and there isn't one. The spout is empty, so the asset looks like an idle can rather than a smoker in use.",
   "The shading is grungy and over-detailed (scratchy texture, heavy dark outlines, dirty highlights on the can and cage). The house style is clean, flat-shaded charcoal, brushed metal and gold, and this is busier than the simple flat characters.",
   "The bellows panel is a muddy olive-brown with black leather. It looks dull next to the house palette and doesn't read clearly as hinged wood boards.",
   "Scale against the person is fine: about the size of the torso, which is believable for a smoker held at the chest. The silhouette reads instantly as a bee smoker (can, wire heat guard, cone spout with nozzle, side bellows). Edges are clean and nothing floats."
  ]
 }
}